{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":62371,"duration_api_ms":94571,"num_turns":5,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"69e03172-31fe-4fa0-9523-ecd0a9661676","total_cost_usd":0.3549535,"usage":{"input_tokens":485,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24327,"cache_read_input_tokens":76634,"output_tokens":2029,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24327,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":93,"outputTokens":5273,"cacheReadInputTokens":251335,"cacheCreationInputTokens":47881,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.11144275000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":485,"outputTokens":2029,"cacheReadInputTokens":76634,"cacheCreationInputTokens":24327,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24351075,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Accept the two amendments with verified defects (alk_budget bookkeeping gap and unconditionally allocating metric()); reject the two whose factual premises are contradicted by the current repository state.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-6a5fe401","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: alk_budget is decremented after AOB (line 296) but NOT after comammox (~line 350), while do_budget IS decremented after both steps. The comammox_alk_cost is computed but never subtracted from alk_budget. This is an asymmetry with the DO budget pattern and a latent accounting bug — if any future step reads the remaining alkalinity budget it will see a stale, over-stated value. The proposed one-line fix is low-risk, consistent with the existing pattern, and closes the invariant gap."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-9ac12929","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: StageTrace::metric() unconditionally calls label.into() (heap String allocation) and pushes a BudgetMetric every time, even when ctx.budget is None and the metrics will never be consumed. In contrast, note() already guards on self.enabled. For nitrogen_cycle alone this is ~5 wasted allocations per tick on the cold path. Adding a guard (either checking a budget_active flag or ctx.budget.is_some()) is behavior-preserving and eliminates unnecessary heap churn when budget tracking is disabled."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-c283b14f","decision":"reject","rationale":"The premise is factually incorrect. crates/tank_core/tests/nitrification_alkalinity.rs exists on disk AND is tracked by git (confirmed via git ls-files). The file is already part of the reviewed change set."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-beff8673","decision":"reject","rationale":"The premise is factually incorrect. NitrogenCycleOutput already exposes both alkalinity_consumed_meq (line 28) and alkalinity_produced_meq (line 34), and the engine emits both as metrics (lines 248-255) and as trace notes (lines 265-271). The claimed gap — that only consumed alkalinity is surfaced — does not exist in the current code. Consumed-vs-returned attribution is already possible with the existing API surface."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f12173a2-007e-4568-89e5-42d7289b065e"}
